                "domain": null,
                "title": "thedrawingshed.org",
                "uri": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE_70MJfZH0sbVuXJq5WYBk3bLL81NpoQbm1gdY4pC9X0OqzXUlPjNKxzTmNCMkCYrdZlY35P8qx4YQGuplkBSkIW-T1MF8jxUzAdNo-5C-z8PP3SvO28C30-dPd1pgHb9qn9EgtHpgcj4qpX90"
              }
            }
          ],
          "grounding_supports": [
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": null,
                "end_index": 175,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The destruction of over a hundred invaluable works of contemporary art in the Momart warehouse fire in Leyton, East London, on May 24, 2004, was far more than a financial loss"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 177,
                "end_index": 432,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "While the financial impact was staggering\u2014estimated between \u00a330 million and \u00a350 million, leading to massive, multi-million-pound insurance payouts and legal settlements\u2014the true toll of the fire was cultural, historical, emotional, and philosophical"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 626,
                "end_index": 792,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "A Cultural and Historical Void\nThe fire consumed iconic works from the **Young British Artists (YBA)** movement, which had redefined the global art scene in the 1990s"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 795,
                "end_index": 937,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Tracey Emin\u2019s** seminal work, *Everyone I Have Ever Slept With 1963\u20131995* (colloquially known as \"the tent\"), was completely destroyed"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 939,
                "end_index": 1129,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The piece, which featured the hand-appliqu\u00e9d names of everyone she had shared a bed with (including family members and lovers), was a cornerstone of the historic 1997 *Sensation* exhibition"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1131,
                "end_index": 1196,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "It was an irreplaceable cultural artifact of 90s confessional art"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                5,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1198,
                "end_index": 1370,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Jake and Dinos Chapman\u2019s** *Hell*, a massive, intricate tableau featuring thousands of miniature, hand-painted Nazi soldiers engaged in apocalyptic violence, was lost"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1372,
                "end_index": 1463,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The work had taken the brothers over two years of painstaking, meticulous labor to complete"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1466,
                "end_index": 1638,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "While some art can theoretically be re-created, art critics argued that original works capture the exact spirit, aims, and social atmosphere of the moment of their creation"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1640,
                "end_index": 1699,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Once lost, that specific zeitgeist cannot be conjured again"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1709,
                "end_index": 1807,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The Tragedy of Deceased Artists\nFor living artists, the fire was devastating but not career-ending"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1809,
                "end_index": 1872,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "For deceased artists, however, the loss was absolute and tragic"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1874,
                "end_index": 1953,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Patrick Heron**, a titan of British modernist abstraction, had died in 1999"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8,
                3,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1955,
                "end_index": 2047,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Over 50 of his paintings, stored in the warehouse and owned by his daughters, were destroyed"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2049,
                "end_index": 2182,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "His daughter, Katherine Heron, described the event as \"another bereavement,\" noting that these works were of international importance"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2184,
                "end_index": 2256,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Helen Chadwick**, an influential conceptual artist, had died in 1996"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2258,
                "end_index": 2347,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Key, unique sculptures that she was working on shortly before her death were lost forever"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6,
                1,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2351,
                "end_index": 2516,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Because these artists were no longer alive to paint or sculpt, the fire permanently erased parts of their artistic legacies, representing a national cultural tragedy"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                9
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2526,
                "end_index": 2664,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The Public Reaction: A Mirror to a Cultural Divide\nPerhaps the most telling aspect of the Momart fire was how the public and media reacted"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6,
                7,
                10
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2666,
                "end_index": 2818,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "While the art establishment mourned, a wave of *schadenfreude* (pleasure derived from another's misfortune) swept through tabloids and public commentary"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                9,
                11
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2822,
                "end_index": 2995,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Because YBA art was notoriously provocative and conceptual, many viewed the destruction of Emin\u2019s tent, Damien Hirst\u2019s pieces, and other avant-garde works with amusement"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                9
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2997,
                "end_index": 3098,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Newspapers and broadcasters openly joked about the fire, asking, *\"Was it just rubbish that burned?\"*"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                12
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3756,
                "end_index": 3967,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Veronica Ryan**, a sculptor who lost works in the fire, later created exhibitions that directly engaged with the absence of her destroyed pieces, using the loss as a springboard for new material explorations"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3970,
                "end_index": 4102,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "### Conclusion\nUltimately, the Momart warehouse fire was not \"merely\" a financial loss because **art is not a mere financial asset**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8,
                6,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 4104,
                "end_index": 4273,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "While insurers settled the bills with tens of millions of pounds, money could not resurrect the physical evidence of human touch, historical momentum, and artistic labor"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6,
                7,
                13
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 4275,
                "end_index": 4433,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The fire remains a stark reminder of the fragile physicality of cultural heritage, proving that when art burns, a piece of our collective history goes with it"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            }
          ],
          "retrieval_metadata": null,
